{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\subset T$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-ph-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:af827cc74c5d1631958adfbd8f3405667991c1f9469e4ee4b21a3688ab4e919c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cde5ff7bd64355a1e8503ffd55377ee12c37a9a1bdbd01583ffaa2d0e0a55ff9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>ph covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes such\nthat <MATH_0004> is locally of finite type and such that for every\naffine open <MATH_0005> there exists a standard ph covering\n<MATH_0006> refining the family\n<MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:252c582fdf345533e9f370470e5ce92112d09a92ac11a45ad56dd818c89a8209", "unit_id": "tag:0DBG:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-standard-ph}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:489a6cc6f4428562dc5083c4b89892cce276724db995b6978e395ac70825f5b4", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA standard ph covering is a ph covering by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7946a11ad51ea157e34b13cafbc1e9d686be748cc43a611871bcdd3f84311a38", "unit_id": "tag:0DBC:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-fppf-ph}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:206cdc0099fef33970bb448ccbcb1ed420a5120c0dd2492c5b329e65c3210bff", "source_text": "A Zariski covering is a ph covering<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>We will see\nin More on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001> that\nfppf coverings (and hence syntomic, smooth, or <ACCENT_0001>tale coverings)\nare ph coverings as well.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:08c4249aa3f01fa82405da0e84cd732342bee47fb9bb16a1fb1989590d882cc5", "unit_id": "tag:0DBH:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-refine-by-standard-ph}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48a8cfa3adc58fd73ded88196466ba20167e97b4d39428c43866345e30c9ceb2", "source_text": "This is true because a Zariski covering of an affine scheme\ncan be refined by a standard ph covering by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fd386c09800e6f91e10ea8291119052dfa86ccbe9e24bb162116b73bedf6babf", "unit_id": "tag:0DBH:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : Y \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{Y \\to X\\}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjective-proper-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:62fbb218167cf8452b0c3cb1ae2e8dfea759d37ddb097b306751a4c167569fe2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aefe11c20951710938f2bdf82bd514098449b1ff09fa64d396bda39e2bcc5e23", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a surjective proper morphism of schemes.\nThen <MATH_0002> is a ph covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4fbb6cb4a58f14ebd1154530ac14cc59c09d27f6bc0cbdf1638bc0d80fe749c1", "unit_id": "tag:0DES:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:abb995395fe8d675a479d76130e30599d047834c06f12f96ac2f35e6ea1a5c90", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0DES:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_i$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{\\coprod_{i \\in I} T_i \\to T\\}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-by-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5dab6ddd2d6d5fb11d535f37088e13d64baccd5280f271a5963212d9e24b5ad3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1513f300696d67aebef93b257e6f3540cafa8e89d5d78e9269c252e8c0bc7db", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a family\nof morphisms such that <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type for all <MATH_0004>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is a ph covering,\n<STRUCT_0003> there is a ph covering which refines <MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is a ph covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f85750991660bc5e3d398d0c87277d505b750a1d082c60ca7e2db412ae4fe50", "unit_id": "tag:0ET9:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{\\coprod_{i \\in I} T_i \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U \\times_T \\coprod_{i \\in I} T_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$j$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nh_j :\nU_j\n\\longrightarrow\nU \\times_T \\coprod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} T_i =\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} U \\times_T T_i\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$U_j$", "MATH_0010": "$U_j = \\coprod_{i \\in I} U_{j, i}$", "MATH_0011": "$h_j|_{U_{j, i}}$", "MATH_0012": "$U_{j, i}$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\times_T T_i$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\{U_{j, i} \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m,\\ i \\in I,\\ U_{j, i} \\not = \\emptyset}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{U \\times_T T_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-ph-covering}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:85bc31e232c1c6e8bca7acbae5e04856f801fb29f3f6d6d6354fa428dd7395c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db1357ee162576ce1d8fd4b5a441bc9176ebfddc4ff356180153dc91d85a66db", "source_text": "The equivalence of (1) and (2) follows immediately from\nDefinition <REF_0001>\nand the fact that a refinement of a refinement is a refinement.\nBecause of the equivalence of (1) and (2) and since\n<MATH_0001> refines <MATH_0002>\nwe see that (1) implies (3). Finally, assume (3) holds.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an affine open and let\n<MATH_0004> be a standard ph covering\nwhich refines <MATH_0005>.\nThis means that for each <MATH_0006> we have a morphism\n<MATH_0007>\nover <MATH_0008>. Since <MATH_0009> is quasi-compact, we get\ndisjoint union decompositions <MATH_0010>\nby open and closed subschemes almost all of which are empty\nsuch that <MATH_0011> maps <MATH_0012> into <MATH_0013>.\nIt follows that\n<MATH_0014>\nis a standard ph covering (small detail omitted) refining\n<MATH_0015>. Thus (1) holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91481538c6f2f6e46b74f80abb5c6befc5704b2dc631ae509568069358285aa5", "unit_id": "tag:0ET9:proof"}
